---
layout: base.njk
---
<section class="hero">
  <div class="wrap hero-in">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <p class="kicker">A deep festival management sim · in development</p>
      <h1>Start with an empty field and $5,000.</h1>
      <p class="lede">{{ site.tagline }}</p>
      <div class="actions">
        {% include "steam-button.njk" %}
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/blog/">Read the devlog</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <figure class="hero-shot">
      <img src="/assets/img/festival.jpg" width="1600" height="1304" alt="A night-time festival seen from above: thousands of visitors around three stages, rows of lit food stalls and toilets.">
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="facts" aria-label="The game in numbers">
  <dl class="wrap facts-in">
    <div><dt>{{ systems.length }}</dt><dd>interlocking systems</dd></div>
    <div><dt>5</dt><dd>staff roles you command directly</dd></div>
    <div><dt>11</dt><dd>kinds of live incident</dd></div>
    <div><dt>100k</dt><dd>visitors the crowd engine handles</dd></div>
  </dl>
</section>

<section class="wrap pitch">
  <div class="pitch-grid">
    <div>
      <h2>Build it</h2>
      <p>Lay down a stage, bars, food stands and toilets. Run cables from generators, keep the power under the limit and leave room for the queues you know are coming.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h2>Book it</h2>
      <p>Plan the night: pick a local act, set ticket prices and open the gates. Hard rock, heavy metal and electronic crowds all want different things.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h2>Survive it</h2>
      <p>A fight by the stage. Someone faints at the front. The bar runs out of beer and the generator shorts out. Your radio does not stop, and every call is yours to answer.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="shots">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 class="section-title">From the current build</h2>
    <div class="shot-grid">
      <figure class="shot shot-wide">
        <img src="/assets/img/concert.jpg" loading="lazy" width="1600" height="856" alt="A small concert in progress: the crowd in front of a pallet stage, radio panel open with a fight and a fainting to deal with.">
        <figcaption>Opening night on a pallet stage. Two calls on the radio already.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="shot">
        <img src="/assets/img/report.jpg" loading="lazy" width="1600" height="856" alt="The event report window listing ticket and bar income, staff wages and incidents.">
        <figcaption>Every show ends with a report card. This one lost $109.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="shot">
        <img src="/assets/img/night.jpg" loading="lazy" width="1600" height="856" alt="A trailer stage, upgraded bar and food stand at night under warm lights.">
        <figcaption>Upgrade the pallets to a trailer stage as your reputation grows.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
    <p class="build-note">Early development screenshots. Some labels are still in Turkish; the game ships in English and Turkish.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="night">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 class="section-title">One night at the venue</h2>
    <p class="section-lede">Building happens on a fast clock, one second for six minutes. When the gates open the clock drops to one second for six seconds, and everything you planned gets tested at walking speed.</p>
    <ol class="timeline">
      <li>
        <span class="tl-time">Days before</span>
        <h3>Plan</h3>
        <p>Book an act, pay the fee up front, set ticket, beer and food prices. The planner shows a demand estimate; your stage size caps it.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="tl-time">18:00</span>
        <h3>Gates open</h3>
        <p>Buses drop visitors at the village stop. The ticket booth queue is the first thing they judge you on.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="tl-time">19:30</span>
        <h3>The rush</h3>
        <p>Needs climb with the clock. Bars and food stands queue up, stock runs down, generators burn fuel and the power draw creeps toward the limit.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="tl-time">20:24</span>
        <h3>Radio</h3>
        <p>A fight near the stage and someone fainted at the front, at the same time. You have one security guard and one medic. Trash is piling up behind the bar.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="tl-time">22:00</span>
        <h3>Last song</h3>
        <p>The crowd heads back to the bus. Staff wages come out of the till.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="tl-time">After</span>
        <h3>Report card</h3>
        <p>Income line by line, costs, average satisfaction, what people were thinking, every incident and whether you handled it. Then the reputation change.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="systems" id="systems">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 class="section-title">Under the hood</h2>
    <p class="section-lede">Venue Simulator is a management game in the old, detailed sense. Every system below is running at the same time, and each one feeds the others: a cheap cable becomes a short circuit, which closes a bar, which grows a queue, which costs you a star, which raises the interest on your loan.</p>
    <div class="sys-grid">
      {%- for s in systems %}
      <article class="sys" id="sys-{{ s.id }}">
        <h3>{{ s.title }}</h3>
        <p>{{ s.summary }}</p>
        <table class="spec">
          {%- for row in s.specs %}
          <tr><th scope="row">{{ row[0] }}</th><td>{{ row[1] }}</td></tr>
          {%- endfor %}
        </table>
        <p class="sys-links"><span>Affects</span>
          {%- for id in s.links %}{% for t in systems %}{% if t.id == id %} <a href="#sys-{{ t.id }}">{{ t.title }}</a>{% endif %}{% endfor %}{% endfor %}
        </p>
      </article>
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>
    <div class="roadmap">
      <h3>In development</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Water:</strong> tanks, pipes and toilets that need them.</li>
        <li><strong>City connections</strong> for power and water, with backup generators for when the grid fails.</li>
        <li><strong>More stalls</strong> for different crowds: street food, cocktails, mulled wine, coffee, merch, sponsor tents.</li>
        <li><strong>Visitor preferences</strong> by genre, season and time of day. Alcohol sells, and it also starts fights.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="wrap latest">
  <div class="latest-head">
    <h2 class="section-title">Devlog</h2>
    <a href="/blog/">All posts →</a>
  </div>
  <ul class="post-list">
    {%- for post in collections.posts | head(3) %}
    <li>
      <time datetime="{{ post.date | isoDate }}">{{ post.date | niceDate }}</time>
      <a href="{{ post.url }}">{{ post.data.title }}</a>
      {% if post.data.description %}<p>{{ post.data.description }}</p>{% endif %}
    </li>
    {%- endfor %}
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="wishlist">
  <div class="wrap wishlist-in">
    <div>
      <h2>Coming to Steam</h2>
      <p>Wishlisting is the single most helpful thing you can do for a small game.{% if not site.steamUrl %} The Steam page opens soon; this button will light up when it does.{% endif %}</p>
    </div>
    {% include "steam-button.njk" %}
  </div>
</section>
